  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 136 AM CDT Tue Aug 25 2026\n\nHot and dry conditions continue through at least the middle of the \nweek, but we will FINALLY have something to talk about. The ridge \nstill continues over the area, with a center somewhere near the Four \nCorners. High temperatures will still be in the 90s along the coast, \nnearing 105 across the Brush Country. A fairly dry air mass will \nhelp regulate our heat index values, keeping them generally in the \nrange of 105-109 across the Brush Country, but expect we could see \nheat index values from 110-113 over isolated location across the \nCoastal Plains and Victoria Crossroads. Expect conditions to be a \nfew degrees warmer Wednesday, so a Heat Advisory may be needed. \nRemember that cumulative heat stress can result in a higher risk of \nheat illness. Please use caution if you are spending time outside. \nDrink plenty of water and take breaks. Don't forget to look before \nyou lock!\n\nThe ridge will finally weaken a bit on the eastern side Wednesday \nnight and Thursday, allowing more moisture to move into the area. \nMeanwhile, a mid-level trough will slide to the south, sneaking in \nunder the ridge and introducing a low (15-40%) chance of showers and \nthunderstorms, mainly east of 281. With the increasing clouds high \ntemperatures across the Victoria Crossroads and along the coast \nshould be a few degrees cooler. While it may only be 2-3 degrees, we \nwill take it!",
